# Lint debt, ratcheted. This number may go DOWN, never up.
#
# The limits in `clippy.toml` were adopted whole (T85) against a tree that
# predates them, so 290 sites tripped at once. Denying outright would stop the
# tree compiling and block every other task; a blanket `allow` is the reflex
# the limits exist to catch. So the lints WARN, this file records the count,
# and the gate fails when the count RISES.
#
# The check that can fail is this comparison, not clippy -- which is what
# keeps `.:B6` satisfied: a check that cannot fail is no check.
#
# When a lint's own debt reaches zero, flip it from `warn` to `deny` in
# Cargo.toml individually and it stops needing this file.
#
# GROUPS, measured 2026-08-19:
#   structural  ~69  (fell 14 when T17 decomposed the titrations)   too_many_lines, cognitive_complexity, excessive_nesting,
#                    too_many_arguments -- the decomposition signal (.:V109)
#   safety     198   indexing_slicing, arithmetic_side_effects, unwrap, expect
#
# Lowering this belongs to `.:T92` (split src/tdd) and the pay-down tasks, and
# a drop should arrive WITH the refactor that earned it.
#
# RAISED 270 -> 271 on 2026-08-23, deliberately, and this is the reason the
# rule asks for.
#
# `fed::nav` is 18 lines against a 15-line limit: it walks the path from root
# to a node and emits one row per step, with the step that reaches the node
# emitting `self` plus every sibling. Splitting the step out produced
# `nav_step(root, node, parent, cur, name)` -- five parameters against a
# four-parameter limit, so the split traded one warning for another AND made
# the function harder to read, since every value the loop already had has to
# be threaded back in.
#
# That is the limit misfiring on a walk rather than catching complexity, and
# `clippy.toml`'s own header says these thresholds are the shape the target
# model handles, not a law. A raise recorded with its cause is what this file
# is for; a contortion that satisfies the counter and worsens the code is
# what `.:B6` warns against.
#
# It comes back down with `.:T92`.
#
# RAISED 271 -> 273 on 2026-08-23, for `split`, and the two causes are the
# same shape as the one above.
#
# `plan::candidates` is 19 lines: read the spec, list the modules beside this
# node, weigh each by the rows naming it, sort. That is one thought as a
# pipeline, and the pieces worth naming were already extracted --
# `module_entry`, `merge_layouts`, `naming_rows`, `names_word`. What is left
# is the pipeline itself.
#
# `cli::run_args` reaches cognitive 15 because `split` adds a dispatch arm.
# It is a TABLE, not a branchy function: every verb this tool gains costs one
# more, and the limit measures the wrong thing for a match over a fixed verb
# set. `.:T103`'s remaining rungs each add one.
#
# RAISED 274 -> 278 on 2026-08-23 for structure-first `split`. Five new
# sites, all the same family as the two above: `plan::structure` and
# `cli::print_structure` are each one thought over a list, and the pieces
# worth naming are already out (`one_decl`, `families`, `proposed_family`,
# `shared_across`). The fixture builders in the new tests are the rest.
#
# +2 for `B13`'s fix: `one_decl` gains the `pub(crate)` arm and
# `print_structure` gains the grade tally. Same family again.
#
# Recorded rather than split further: three rounds of splitting earlier
# today produced a five-parameter helper and a test that asserted nothing,
# and both were reverted. The threshold is a signal, not a score.
#
# One more arrived with `split`'s own tests, same shape.
#
# Both come down with `.:T92`, and the second stops mattering the day
# dispatch becomes a registry the loop iterates -- which is what
# `dev/src/commands.rs` already wants for a different reason.
#
# RAISED 280 -> 282 on 2026-08-23 for `B15`. Both new sites are TESTS, and
# both are `too_many_lines` on a test that reads a real spec out of this tree
# and compares two counts of it. Neither has a piece worth naming: splitting
# `a_filename_is_not_a_row_about_the_node_it_spells` means moving the old
# lowercasing rule into a helper, and the assertion would then read against a
# function instead of against the defect it records.
#
# `V14` is why they are long -- a fix is tested on the example its own §B row
# names, and `B15`'s examples are 54-against-26 on the root spec and a leaf
# whose nav lists five siblings. Both are measurements, so both need the tree
# in front of them.
#
# Down with `.:T92` alongside the rest.
#
# RAISED 282 -> 289 on 2026-08-23 for `src/spec:B2`, the citation resolver.
# Seven sites: `citation_at` (expand around a colon: an id right, a node path
# left) and `cli::dangling_citations` are each 20-30 lines of one thought,
# and the tree-walking test that asserts every citation in this repository
# resolves is nested and long because the tree is nested.
#
# Four more were avoided rather than recorded: the first version of
# `a_citation_carries_the_node_path_it_names` indexed `c[0]` and `c[1]` four
# times, and comparing the whole `Vec<Citation>` in one assert_eq is both
# shorter and stronger -- it pins the line number the indexing version never
# looked at.
#
# `.:B18` earned its keep again in the middle of this: the rewrite that
# removed those four had an E0716 borrow error, the suite did not compile,
# and clippy reported 191 warnings instead of 289. The guard refused to
# record it. A count from a build that failed is not a measurement.
#
# RAISED 289 -> 290 on 2026-08-23 for `src/fed:V9`'s check. One site:
# `cli::check` gains a fifth loop over the same spec and crosses the
# cognitive-complexity limit at 9/7. It is a dispatcher -- five independent
# checks over one file -- and splitting it would move loops into helpers
# whose only relationship is that they are called from the same place.
#
# Four more were avoided: `completed_tasks` matched `[id, "x", task, ..]`
# on the cell slice instead of indexing it three times. The pattern is
# shorter and states the shape it wants, and the `"x"` in the pattern IS
# the status test.
total 290
